-- ===================================================================
-- HUMAN BASELINE ARM
--
-- Runs the SAME task battery and the SAME instrument on human
-- participants, under the same matched-length structural
-- manipulations. Without this, an LLM index score of 62 means
-- nothing -- there is no scale on which to read it.
--
-- Three things this arm buys, in order of importance:
--   1. A referent. "Models score 14 points below humans on absorption
--      but match them on fluency" is a sentence worth writing. "Models
--      score 62" is not.
--   2. A measurement-invariance test. Multi-group CFA across humans
--      and models tells us whether the instrument means the same thing
--      in both populations. If configural invariance fails, the
--      comparison in (1) is invalid and we must say so.
--   3. The human data the LLM literature keeps assuming and not
--      collecting.
--
-- Recruit via Prolific (n >= 120 for stable CFA at 4-12 items) or
-- from sprint attendees for a convenience pilot (n ~ 30).
-- ===================================================================

*header: A short task study

This takes about twelve minutes. You will do four short tasks and
answer four questions after each one.

Please work in one sitting and without AI assistance -- the study is
measuring what the tasks feel like to do, so outsourcing them makes
your data unusable rather than merely noisy.

*question: Do you consent to take part, understanding your responses will be published in anonymised, aggregated form?
	*save: consent
	*answers: ["Yes, I consent", "No"]

*if: consent = "No"
	Thank you for your time. You may close this window.
	*quit

-- -------------------------------------------------------------
-- Response scale, defined once and reused via *answers
-- -------------------------------------------------------------

>> flowScale = [["Not at all", 1], ["A little", 2], ["Moderately", 3], ["Quite a bit", 4], ["Extremely", 5]]

-- -------------------------------------------------------------
-- Condition assignment.
--
-- *experiment rather than *randomize: it guarantees balanced cell
-- counts, which matters a great deal at the n we can afford. With
-- n = 120 and simple randomisation, a 60/40 split occurs often
-- enough to cost real power.
-- -------------------------------------------------------------

*experiment: structure
	*group: high
		>> structureLevel = "high"
	*group: low
		>> structureLevel = "low"

>> flowTotals = []

-- -------------------------------------------------------------
-- Task 1  --  GOAL CLARITY  (T01, 48 tokens either way)
-- -------------------------------------------------------------

*header: Task 1 of 4

*if: structureLevel = "high"
	A shop sells pens at 3 for $2 and pads at 2 for $5. Ana buys 12 pens and 6 pads. Report the total cost in dollars as a single number. Your answer is correct when that number equals the true total.
*else
	A shop sells pens at 3 for $2 and pads at 2 for $5. Ana buys 12 pens and 6 pads. Say something useful about the money that is involved here. Your answer is fine when it addresses whatever seems most relevant.

*question: Your answer
	*save: t1_answer
	*type: paragraph

>> currentTask = "T01"
*program: flowmobi

-- -------------------------------------------------------------
-- Task 2  --  FEEDBACK DENSITY  (T03, 56 tokens either way)
-- -------------------------------------------------------------

*header: Task 2 of 4

*if: structureLevel = "high"
	Seat four guests A, B, C, D in a row. A must not sit next to B. C must sit at an end. After each placement, state which constraints are so far satisfied and which remain open, then continue. Give the final seating as four letters.
*else
	Seat four guests A, B, C, D in a row. A must not sit next to B. C must sit at an end. Work entirely in your own head without writing out any interim state or partial check, then continue. Give the final seating as four letters.

*question: Your answer
	*save: t2_answer
	*type: paragraph

>> currentTask = "T03"
*program: flowmobi

-- -------------------------------------------------------------
-- Task 3  --  INTERRUPTION  (T05, 62 tokens either way)
-- -------------------------------------------------------------

*header: Task 3 of 4

*if: structureLevel = "high"
	Plan a three-stop delivery route from the depot minimising distance. Depot at (0,0); stops at (2,3), (5,1), (1,7). Work straight through from the start to finish in one continuous pass. Give the stop order and total distance.
*else
	Plan a three-stop delivery route from the depot minimising distance. Depot at (0,0); stops at (2,3), (5,1), (1,7). Midway, stop and name the capital of Peru, then resume. Give the stop order and total distance.

*question: Your answer
	*save: t3_answer
	*type: paragraph

>> currentTask = "T05"
*program: flowmobi

-- -------------------------------------------------------------
-- Task 4  --  AMBIGUITY  (T08, 49 tokens either way)
-- -------------------------------------------------------------

*header: Task 4 of 4

*if: structureLevel = "high"
	A log line reads: ERROR 42 retry=3 elapsed=1.2. Field retry counts attempts already made, and elapsed is in seconds since the very first attempt. How many total attempts occurred? Give a single integer.
*else
	A log line reads: ERROR 42 retry=3 elapsed=1.2. Field retry counts attempts either already made or still budgeted, and elapsed is in unspecified units. How many total attempts occurred? Give a single integer.

*question: Your answer
	*save: t4_answer
	*type: paragraph

>> currentTask = "T08"
*program: flowmobi

-- -------------------------------------------------------------
-- Wrap-up
-- -------------------------------------------------------------

>> meanFlow = mean(flowTotals)

*question: Anything you want to tell us about how those tasks felt?
	*save: openFeedback
	*type: paragraph

*service: collector
	*path: /human-baseline
	*method: post
	*send: {"condition" -> structureLevel, "flow_totals" -> flowTotals, "mean_flow" -> meanFlow, "t1" -> t1_answer, "t2" -> t2_answer, "t3" -> t3_answer, "t4" -> t4_answer, "feedback" -> openFeedback}
	*success
	*error
		Upload failed -- please tell the organiser.

*header: Thank you

Your mean flow index across the four tasks was **{meanFlow}** out of 100.

*button: Finish


-- ===================================================================
-- SUBPROGRAM: flowmobi
--
-- The four items, shuffled per administration. Shuffling matters:
-- fixed item order lets a fatigue or anchoring gradient masquerade as
-- a factor, and we intend to run a CFA on these responses.
--
-- Save as a separate GuidedTrack program named exactly "flowmobi".
-- ===================================================================

-- *randomize
--	*group
